      "message": "Explanation from Caveh: \"timeout\" is not a hard delay -- it is an upper limit to sleep until another EVENT arrives. In some situations, sending a HARD_RESET will generate an immediate ALERT.\n\nUpon arrival of another ALERT \u003d\u003d(gpio reset, register cleared, converted to)\u003d\u003d\u003e EVENT \u003d\u003d\u003e PD-TASK call, this \"timeout\" is reduced to 0 and the loop resumes. It will then attempt to transmit another HARD_RESET, begin a 10ms \"timeout\", said HARD_RESET generates an immediate ALERT, \"timeout\" is reduced to 0, etc.\n\n(repeat ad nauseum).",
